## Complete Operation Count

```
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
TOTAL OPERATIONS TO ADD 1 NODE TO A 13-NODE GRAPH
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

PHASE                        OPERATIONS      NOTES
────────────────────────     ──────────      ──────────────
Atomization (text → node)    ~10             LLM call for parsing
Placement — Layer classify   57              50 rules + 7 centroids
Placement — Family assign    6               3 lookups + 3 centroids
Signal 1 — Entity match      16              3 lookups + 13 scores
Signal 2 — Embedding sim     14 (10K FLOP)   1 embed + 13 cosines
Signal 3 — Graph proximity   55              13 checks + 29 BFS + 13 agg
Signal 4 — Layer pattern     26              13 lookups + 13 scores
Score fusion                 152             91 arith + 48 sort + 13 filter
Conflict detection           35 + 1 LLM      10 pairwise comparisons
────────────────────────     ──────────      ──────────────
GRAND TOTAL                  371 operations  + 2 LLM calls
                             + ~10K FLOPs    (embedding math)
```

```
BROKEN DOWN BY SCALING BEHAVIOR:

Operations that scale with n (graph size):
  Entity scoring:        O(n) — score each existing node
  Embedding similarity:  O(n) — cosine vs each existing node
  Graph BFS:             O(a × b^d) — a anchors, b branching, d depth
  Layer pattern:         O(n) — score each existing node
  Score fusion:          O(n) — compute for each + O(n log n) sort
  Conflict detection:    O(K) — compare top-K candidates

Operations that are constant:
  Atomization:           O(1) — one LLM call regardless of graph size
  Layer classification:  O(1) — fixed number of layers
  Family assignment:     O(F) — number of families (grows slowly)

DOMINANT COST: O(n) for signals + O(K) for conflict checks
```

