## Part 8: The Real-World Quality Difference

### The Re-Generation Problem

```
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
WHAT HAPPENS WHEN GENERATED CODE IS WRONG?
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

FLAT MARKDOWN:

  Developer: "The upload handler doesn't support chunked upload."

  Action: Re-prompt with ALL specs + ALL generated code +
          "fix the upload handler to support chunked upload"

  Token cost: 764 (specs) + 3,760 (all code) + 100 (fix instruction)
            = 4,624 tokens input + ~800 tokens regenerated output
            = 5,424 tokens for ONE fix

  Risk: The re-generation may FIX chunked upload but
        BREAK something else that was working. The model
        must hold all code in context while modifying one part.

  Second fix: If the fix broke something, another round:
    = 5,424 + 5,424 = 10,848 tokens for TWO fixes

  Typical fix cycles: 2-4 rounds
  Total cost: 10,000 - 22,000 tokens to get everything right


GRAPH-BASED:

  Developer: "The upload handler doesn't support chunked upload."

  Identify: This is TASK 3 (Upload Handler).
  Relevant specs: F1, F4, F5, F6, F7, A3.

  Action: Re-run TASK 3 ONLY.

  Token cost: 650 (task input) + 800 (regenerated output)
            = 1,450 tokens for ONE fix

  Risk: Re-generation only affects uploadService.ts.
        ALL OTHER files remain unchanged and consistent.
        No risk of breaking share links, tests, or routes.

  If TASK 3 output changes its interface:
    Re-run TASK 5 (routes) which depends on TASK 3.
    Additional cost: ~1,330 tokens.
    Total: 2,780 tokens.

  Typical fix cycles: 1-2 rounds (focused context = fewer errors)
  Total cost: 1,450 - 4,200 tokens to get it right


REGENERATION TOKEN COMPARISON:

  Scenario              Flat Markdown    Graph-Based    Savings
  ──────────────────    ─────────────    ───────────    ───────
  1 spec wrong,          5,424           1,450          73%
  1 fix needed

  1 spec wrong,         10,848           2,780          74%
  2 fixes needed

  3 specs wrong,        16,272           4,350          73%
  separate fixes

  Major refactor        22,000           6,500          70%
  (4 rounds)

  THE GRAPH SAVES 70-75% ON REGENERATION COSTS.

  This is arguably MORE IMPORTANT than initial generation
  cost because regeneration happens MORE OFTEN.
  In practice, first-pass code generation rarely produces
  perfect code. The fix-iterate cycle IS the real workflow.
```

