```

```
THE ULTIMATE INSIGHT:
═════════════════════

The SDD-Compiler is NOT a single system.
It is THREE systems working together:

  1. A DETERMINISTIC COMPILER (structured vectors,
     graph algorithms, matrix operations)
     → Handles: entity matching, conflict detection,
       task grouping, impact analysis, completeness checks
     → Cost: zero tokens, microseconds
     → Accuracy: 100% for well-encoded specs

  2. A LOCAL ML SYSTEM (embeddings, 7B models, FAISS)
     → Handles: semantic similarity, classification,
       novel entity detection, alias resolution
     → Cost: zero tokens, milliseconds
     → Accuracy: 80-90%

  3. A CLOUD LLM (frontier model API)
     → Handles: semantic understanding of complex specs,
       ambiguity resolution, CODE GENERATION
     → Cost: tokens (minimized by 1 and 2)
     → Accuracy: 90-95%

  Each system handles what it does BEST.
  The deterministic system does the MATH.
  The local ML does the PATTERN MATCHING.
  The cloud LLM does the UNDERSTANDING.
```

